msgid "lore/description/Medium_02"
msgstr ""
"Rising above the endless fields stands an old wooden windmill. It looks fragile, but the locals insist it's survived more artillery hits over the years than any of the stone buildings nearby. Its silhouette has long served as a landmark for birds, travelers, and even pilots flying high above the countryside. The three friends stopped here to rest and spent quite some time debating what was more impressive: the windmill's age or its ability to withstand everything happening around it.\n"
"\n"
"\"You hear a dog too?\"\n"
"\"Been hearing it for ten minutes now.\"\n"
"\"But there's nobody here.\"\n"
"\"Maybe it's some kind of local legend?\"\n"
"\"Maybe. Or maybe it just knows better than we do where to hide from artillery.\""

msgid "lore/description/Medium_05"
msgstr ""
"The Pearl River was the final stop on their journey. Here, time seemed to slow down on its own. Emerald hillsides, cascading waterfalls, ancient pagodas, and mist rising above the water turned the landscape into a living painting. Even the most talkative members of the group fell silent for a while to take in the view. Of all the places they had visited, this was the one that made them think about tanks the least. The Pearl River reminded them that sometimes the most valuable discoveries are made not on the battlefield, but on the way there.\n"
"\n"
"\"What are those strange trees?\"\n"
"\"They're ginkgo trees. Often found near temples and pagodas.\"\n"
"\"No wonder it's so beautiful around here.\"\n"
"\"Yeah. This is the first map we've visited where we haven't talked about tanks at all.\"\n"
"\"Then this place really is something special...\""

msgid "lore/description/Medium_16"
msgstr ""
"Once, this lighthouse guided ships through the dangerous coastal rocks. Today, it serves a different kind of traveler. It's said that its light can be seen by tankers from miles away, and always attracts the most curious scouts. Locals joke that whoever reaches the lighthouse first already controls half the coast. That's why the three travelers spent more time here than anywhere else. The view from a place long considered the heart of the Cliff was too breathtaking to leave behind.\n"
"\n"
"\"Funny how the lighthouse seems to attract light tanks.\"\n"
"\"And fireflies, too.\"\n"
"\"So that's why they always rush here first. They probably think it's their natural habitat.\""

msgid "lore/description/Medium_21"
msgstr ""
"The travelers' journey led them to a small town lost among the sands. The wind drifted lazily through the deserted streets, carrying dust between the buildings and evoking images of a town alive with activity. Now, it seemed to exist somewhere between the past and the present, its squares, alleyways, and marketplaces frozen in time under endless desert sun. There was no reason to rush here. Every turn revealed a new view, and every street seemed to tell the story of the people who had once called this place home.\n"
"\n"
"\"You know what color camouflage proved surprisingly effective in the desert?\"\n"
"\"...Sand?\"\n"
"\"Pink.\"\n"
"\"Pink?\"\n"
"\"That's right. At sunrise and sunset, it would blend into the landscape better than anyone expected.\"\n"
"\"So all these years, we've been underestimating the power of glamour...\""

msgid "lore/name/Medium_02"
msgstr "Malinovka: The Old Windmill"

msgid "lore/name/Medium_05"
msgstr "Pearl River: The Valley"

msgid "lore/name/Medium_16"
msgstr "Cliff: The Lighthouse"

msgid "lore/name/Medium_21"
msgstr "Sand River: The Desert Town"

